==English==

===Etymology===
{{etystub}}

The unit of measure sense is from that quantity's often being the amount a person must drink if taking a do-over in a drinking game.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{rfv-sense}} [[mulligan stew#English|Mulligan stew]].
#* '''1956''', [[w:Nelson Algren|Nelson Algren]], [[w:A Walk on the Wild Side (novel)|''A Walk on the Wild Side'']], 1998 paperback edition, ISBN 0374525323, pages 90–91&nbsp;[http://books.google.com/books?id=abo0A-o8QUYC&pg=PA90&dq=mulligan]:
#*: Another afternoon Dove jungled up with four others beside a creek.{{...}} A couple of the boys got a '''mulligan''' going. Dove lay naked in the creek smoking a cigarette and smelling the '''mulligan'''.
# {{golf}} An unpenalized chance to re-take a stroke that went awry.
#: ''If you lose your drive in the water, take a '''mulligan''' and try again.''
# {{rfv-sense}} A second [[chance]].
#: ''Don't do poorly in your first interview; you won't get a '''mulligan'''.''
# {{rfv-sense}} {{informal}} A unit of measure equal to 62.5 [[milliliter]]s, or 2.5 shots, of alcohol.
#: ''Tom couldn't handle the shot of tequila, so he had to do a '''mulligan''' of port.''

